  "id": "COMPOUND:26119 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between N,3,5,8-Tetrabromo-6-(Bromomethyl)Naphthalen-2-Amine and CD70 antigen, mediated through DMS-79. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple molecules, including 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester and Cinnamtannin A2, both of which are known to interact with CD70 antigen. The consistent presence of DMS-79 as a common target across these pathways indicates a potential mechanism involving receptor engagement or signaling pathways that are influenced by these compounds. The high scores in all three paths suggest a robust and reliable connection, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence points to a possible role in modulating immune responses, as CD70 is a critical surface marker on B cells and is involved in immune cell activation and signaling.",
